      "id": 1,
      "text": "Founded as Franklin in 1837, the village later adopted its current name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bismarck%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1843, brothers John and Samuel Myers built a grist mill near Franklin, sparking the rise of Myersville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bismarck%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the C&EI Railroad arrived in 1872, it ran one and a half miles east, prompting Bismarck to relocate toward the tracks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bismarck%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "On September 13, 1997, Bismarck marked its 125th birthday with a parade, contests, and historical exhibits.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bismarck%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In August 2017, the Newell Township Historical Society opened Bismarck's Municipal History Museum inside the village's old bank house.",
